I was on nethack1.devnull.net as eidolos2.

Well, I pressed ! and the screen cleared, displayed the introductory
"Welcome, eidolos2, to the NetHack Tournament 2006". It gave a "Active
game detected. Attempting to save." Then it said: "Would you like to
return to NetHack?(y/n)". I continually pressed y, and it eventually
said "Game saved." "Press <Return> to begin."

Then the screen cleared and displayed the introductory "Welcome,
eidolos2, to the NetHack Tournament 2006" again. It then seemed to
restore my game (at least I got a "Restoring save file..."). But it was
unresponsive until I hit the spacebar enough times. Then I got a "Shall
I pick a character's race, role, gender and alignment for you?". I'm
not sure what I pressed at this point, but then it said "Really quit?
[yn] (n)" at the top of the screen and a @ at the position my character
was in the game. That is, with the "Shall I pick.." still displayed.

I hit some more keys (again, I dunno which ones, probably just the
space bar) and my old game seemed to be restored. Elation! But as I
pressed keys the screen suddenly shifted to a new game. They were going
back and forth. I ended up saving the first game, I think, then
quitting the second game. When I tried to log in again I got another
"Shall I pick..."

So it's pretty clear that I had two games going at the same time
(probably because the shell escape boots up a new nethack process).

The fix would be to disable the ! command (just like ^Z is disabled).

The entire game's ttyrec (including the wonky end) is at
http://sartak.katron.org/nh/devnull.ttyrec.bz2

Don't get me wrong, I appreciate the time, effort, and money you guys
are putting into this tournament. But it's very disheartening to lose
such a good character who clearly would have been well off in the
running for first ascension. Especially after the annoyance of
registering. Oh well. :)

